{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness","id":1138733,"title":"Elseworlds - DC Chronicles of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-08T15:59:04-07:00","id":1138733,"title":"Elseworlds - DC Chronicles of Darkness","content":"Like I did with Marvel, it could be fun to speculate about who would be what if the DC Universe also took place in the Chronicles of Darkness. Like with Marvel, I may try to write some CofD crossover fiction at some point, but for now, lets just have fun brainstorming.<br /> <br /> As before, I'm totally open to people discussing multiple possibilities for who characters would be and how the world would work. Interpretations could range from obvious (Etrigan is a Demon, Batman is a mortal with shit-ton of fighting merits) to plausible (Captain Atom as a Mage of Matter and Life, the Flash as Master of Space) to really out there (Joker as a Beast that genuinely wants to help people but keeps getting demonized by Heroes). In my eyes, all of those are equally valid and worthy of discussion.<br /> <br /> Also, if you were to make an expanded universe out of a DC/CofD crossover, who would you start with and how would you go about it?<br /> <br /> So, what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 09-08-2017, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T17:08:05-07:00","id":1138753,"title":"","content":"Ra's al Ghul seems like a classic Immortal. Instead of a Blood Bather he has his Lazarus Pits, with grants a debilitating Madness Condition when used. The Tribe of Ubu, League of Shadows and League of Assassins, sometimes different things, sometimes different names for the same, are Mystery Cults with him at the head. High occult and science.<br /> <br /> I know people prefer to go with gamelines, but a lot of the villains are easily Urged, Ridden or outright Claimed, like Poison Ivy and Swamp Thing, Animal Man and so forth. You could probably do them as Deviants but we don't really know the Deviant capability yet. Vixen has a Skinchanger amulet that grants her the attributes of animals. Manbat could be a thing from Skinchangers or a Deviant.<br /> <br /> Simon Dark is an Extempore of Gotham. Kafka one of the Unclean. I like to imagine daemonites as an extraterrestrial host, trapped here when Pangaea fell.<br /> <br /> While I could see an argument for the New Gods as Mages, some of them seem like they would be more fitting as outright Supernal beings. The Highfather as an Oracle, Darkseid is effectively all the Exarchs, with the other New Gods of Apokalips lesser reflections of him. If you went by the argument that the Exarchs are, in turn, lesser shades of some darker Tyranny, it would be an easy to go to Darkseid for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2017, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T17:56:28-07:00","id":1138762,"title":"","content":"I prefer to have Batman and Joker as a Hunter and a Slasher, respectively. However, they could also work as Beasts (an Ugallu Nemesis and Namtaru Ravager, respectively). Many of Batman's Rogues Gallery work as Slashers or Deviants.<br /> <br /> Superman works well as an Unchained. A Guardian Inquisitor, most likely. The Clark Kent persona is his main Cover, the Man Of Steel is his Demonic Form and the Fortress Of Solitude is a super Bolthole.<br /> <br /> The various versions of the Flash are either Deviants or Mages with a Time/Forces Legacy.<br /> <br /> Mr. Mxyzptlk is either an epic True Fae or an Archmage.<br /> <br /> Solomon Grundy is a Promethean, likely an Extempore.<br /> <br /> John Constantine is a Mastigos Apostate with 2 dots across several Arcana, surprisingly decent Wisdom and high Gnosis + tons of Praxes to compensate for his lack of Rotes.<br /> <br /> Wonder Woman at first seemed like a Galateid Promethean to me, but I don't think she struggled with anything like Disquiet/Wastelands/Pilgrimage. It is possible that she is an unique creation of the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> The Green Lanterns are likely Mages of the Adamatine Arrow with a Prime/Mind Legacy.<br /> <br /> Martian Manhunter is...I don't know, some kind of benevolent Idigam? How would that even work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T19:16:04-07:00","id":1138780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470005-gotham-city-of-secrets\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470005-gotham-city-of-secrets\"> Gotham: City of Secrets - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470005-gotham-city-of-secrets\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/470005-gotham-city-of-secrets </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It's been 2 WoD forums since I've seen a Batman/Gotham setting thread so here we go. [tape starts] So what do you want to know? ... Everyone says Gotham and I've </div> </div> </div><br /> Did this ages ago, I've explained it a bit in post 714 of the think of a fictional character thread.<br /> Alternitive take is Batman is a True Fay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T22:28:53-07:00","id":1138806,"title":"","content":"Benevolent aren't necessarily evil, they're more alien. They really don't like werewolves, though.<br /> <br /> Eclipso would be a good example of an idigam. I realize now that as a sort of 'evil entity' this goes against my previous statement, but he exists in a coalesced form, his Black Diamond shards capable of turning people into heralds and other servants to promote his goal. The Blue Scarab might be a good example of a lower-powered idigam.<br /> <br /> They could be another way to do the Lantern Corps. Each Lantern Central Power Battery being a sort of lair for these entities associated with different emotions, the ringbearers being heralds granted with some of the idigam's Influences. Talking about a Universe-wide cult powered by entities who are likewise universal embodiments of different emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T23:35:09-07:00","id":1138811,"title":"","content":"Superman and Lex Luthor I would view as a modern classical example of the relationship as Beast and Hero. <br /> <br /> Lex checks out on many of the traits of modern Heroes as described in BtP: selfish and arrogant, believes metahumans, especially Superman, as being detrimental to human/mortal society, he's one of the few that's truly qualified to take them down, but has no issue using whatever means necessary...even if it means coercion, bribery, and violence to bring down metahumans. And how deep down, he has his own self-loathing on wanting to be like Supes, to get all the fame and glory for himself. Not because he's altruistic about keeping metahumans in line (unlike, say, Amanda Waller).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T00:22:48-07:00","id":1138820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1138811#post1138811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Superman and Lex Luthor I would view as a modern classical example of the relationship as Beast and Hero. <br /> <br /> Lex checks out on many of the traits of modern Heroes as described in BtP: selfish and arrogant, believes metahumans, especially Superman, as being detrimental to human/mortal society, he's one of the few that's truly qualified to take them down, but has no issue using whatever means necessary...even if it means coercion, bribery, and violence to bring down metahumans. And how deep down, he has his own self-loathing on wanting to be like Supes, to get all the fame and glory for himself. Not because he's altruistic about keeping metahumans in line (unlike, say, Amanda Waller).</div> </div> </div> </div>I also think this is a very good fit, although Demon!Superman works well too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T04:48:12-07:00","id":1138848,"title":"","content":"Amanda Waller using supernatural creatures as a spear point for TFV to protect Americas interests, try and get a ghoul into congress and you can expect a visit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T20:32:54-07:00","id":1139090,"title":"","content":"I've been running a DC based CofD game for almost a decade now, it's a lot of fun. Some concepts gave me headaches to fit in (Lantern Corps, I'm looking at you) but all of the players enjoy it. We started it set in 2012 with villains. Somehow we ended up at 1999 with the teen titans. Good times. I did take some stranger takes on some characters, and a few of the players went even stranger with the PC heroes and villins, but.. we do our homework.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T21:32:15-07:00","id":1139095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1139090#post1139090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been running a DC based CofD game for almost a decade now, it's a lot of fun. Some concepts gave me headaches to fit in (Lantern Corps, I'm looking at you) but all of the players enjoy it. We started it set in 2012 with villains. Somehow we ended up at 1999 with the teen titans. Good times. I did take some stranger takes on some characters, and a few of the players went even stranger with the PC heroes and villins, but.. we do our homework.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lanterns are limited by creativity, right? Sounds like several legacies Mages, with Green Lanterns as a legacy specializing in Forces. I'm not nearly as verse in the others to comment on them though. DC needs to hurry up and get a Marvel Unlimited-style subscription up and running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T22:51:49-07:00","id":1139108,"title":"","content":"For the most part. There's some ridiculous Lantern stuff out there. Green Rings are for the most part the simplest, will it, it comes into being as green energy. The Black Lantern Rings return the dead to life, as sort of life-draining zombies. The Orange Lantern Ring lets you absorb the 'identity' of a person and then make them as a construct. The Blue Lantern ring has a special power to refill the energy of and supercharge other rings. The Red Ring replaces the bearers heart, turning their blood into fire and 'red energy,' which burns. The potential is limitless, but limits pop up all the time.<br /> <br /> If you want to go mage they would be attainments, I guess. But it's still hard to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T22:55:45-07:00","id":1139109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1138811#post1138811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Superman and Lex Luthor I would view as a modern classical example of the relationship as Beast and Hero.<br /> <br /> Lex checks out on many of the traits of modern Heroes as described in BtP: selfish and arrogant, believes metahumans, especially Superman, as being detrimental to human/mortal society, he's one of the few that's truly qualified to take them down, but has no issue using whatever means necessary...even if it means coercion, bribery, and violence to bring down metahumans. And how deep down, he has his own self-loathing on wanting to be like Supes, to get all the fame and glory for himself. Not because he's altruistic about keeping metahumans in line (unlike, say, Amanda Waller).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go so far as to specifically say that Superman is specifically an Anakim Tyrant who establishes dominance by making himself the biggest hero around. His Brood includes Obrimos Green Lantern, Levinquick Changeling Flash, Were-bat Batman, Tammuz Wonder Woman (going with the &quot;made from clay&quot; origin), Order-Claimed Doctor Fate, Deviant Plastic Man, and Noble Shazam (specifically a Champion of Cups). Among so many others. And I'm kind of mixing JSA and JLA here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T22:56:49-07:00","id":1139110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1139109#post1139109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noble Shazam (specifically a Champion of Cups).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fansplat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T04:58:33-07:00","id":1139145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1139110#post1139110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a fansplat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Princess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T14:11:21-07:00","id":1139273,"title":"","content":"For the Lantern Corps, I did go with a mage legacy--specifically, Seers of the Throne, with the &quot;guardians of the universe'' being their euphemism for the Exarchs. They're a Prime/mind based legacy based on construction of eidolons and such, with Rings and Lanterns largely serving as mana batteries. The entities within the rings are either powerful goetia of the emotions, or perhaps even Supernal, though some (Larfleeze especially) seem more like archmasters.<br /> <br /> Superman was a shoe in for me due to crossover that was already in the works, but.. my justice lineup...<br /> <br /> Batman: a one man tier 3.5 Hunter conspiracy, that pretends to be an unknown supernatural being. There is no Batgirl or Batwoman--rather, all three dress as the Bat to make it seem Omnipresent, even sometimes during the same fight (thus allowing the ''solo'' Batman to use tactics). Dick Grayson was infected with the Mekhet Curse, Jason Todd is a Bound and Torn Reaper, Alfred is a ''retired'' angelic agent..<br /> <br /> Wonder Woman, rather unshockingly, is a Galateid Promethean. She hasn't been directly introduced yet, and her creation, Donna Troy, has been seeking her out on the Pilgrimage. Wonder Woman has only been seen through athanors and elpis visions, flashbacks, and the like. <br /> <br /> Aquaman is an Atlantean-faithed mage, destined to lead the Consilium after he returns from exile. Topo is his familiar, and he is excavating an undersea Atlanta ruin to use as his sanctum. One of his ''lads'', Tempest, has recently become a Tamer of Rivers, like Tula before him. Ocean Master is a scelesti. Meta hasn't been introduced yet, but I'm leaning towards Changeling or Beast (with kinship to mages, changeling, and Atlantis).<br /> <br /> The Flash, so far, is likely a demon, but so far he is a mystery. Bart Allen is a Fractal, so its possible that the ''lightning bolt'' was the Flash's fall, and Barry Allen and the job as a lab tech was retroactively added as Cover.<br /> <br /> The Arrow is a changeling of the Winter Court, likely a Soldier and Woodwalker. I went with a mixture of Link and Legolas, but with more darkness and cold oriented, evergreens and starry nights. The Island was his durance, and he never met his Keeper. Though a fetch of him was made, it was made incorrectly--it came out the wrong age, with no memories, in a native American tribal reserve. He was raised as Roy Harper, who would eventually find The Arrow and have a troubled relationship with him. <br /> <br /> Cyborg is a Deviant, likely Loyal.<br /> <br /> The Martian Manhunter hasn't been revealed, but due to shapeshifting prowess and an unusual bane and backstory, I'm slating him as a Huntsman, though not one sent to capture any of the Lost associated with the teams. Miss Martian is a changeling of the same keeper, but unlikely to be the Manhunter's target unless I can make their familial or romantic affection in the end. <br /> <br /> Hawkman is a falcon headed Maa'kep who may have chronologically been the first Justice Society member, having been part of something akin to it since the beginning of human society. He still has memories of the Su-Menent that performed the Rite upon him, and fears he has died at its hands many times since. Hawkgirl is a psychopomp Angel that has inserted itself into Hackman's life and memories as his ''handler'', and is secretly trying to use the Justice League as the God-machine's secret task force and brute squad. She will eventually be discovered to be a traitor and spy, and will have to choose between loyalty to her alien agenda or loyalty to her earthly allies and lover.<br /> <br /> Ironically, I haven't read Princess yet, but somehow that does seem like it'd be a great fit for Shazam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T15:08:03-07:00","id":1139283,"title":"","content":"It might seem weird but would the green lantern corps work as a Hunter the Vigil conspiracy with the ring being an endowment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T15:37:35-07:00","id":1139288,"title":"","content":"It could, it would just be a pretty versatile one as a straight conversion.<br /> <br /> There was a nice MUD that had the Green Lantern Corps as a guild, basically a class that had things summed up mechanically. They changed it for legal reasons but the basics are still there. Again, a lot of powers. I think they shine through a lens instead of using their power through a ring.<br /> <br /> That said, there's a lot of power. <a href=\"https://wiki.lostsouls.org/Category:Lightbringer_Volitions\" target=\"_blank\">Creating projections, small and big, including animated 'minions,' energy blasts, creating armor and weapons, translating languages, 'scanning' things, holding things in stasis.</a><br /> <br /> For Chronicles of Darkness, it would be easier to have things limited by dot range, with the dot signifying your mastery of Willpower or whatever, each dot allowing you to do more and more, even if that's not quite how it's portrayed in the comics.<br /> <br /> For a more 'real' conversion, you would just make the rings artifacts. They are willing to choose wildly different lifeforms as bearers, people from all over the moral spectrum. Then have the individual able to deal with its powers based on their own Attributes and effected by Skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-10-2017, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T22:44:02-07:00","id":1139360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1139273#post1139273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically, I haven't read Princess yet, but somehow that does seem like it'd be a great fit for Shazam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, definitely. An idealistic kid who gains a super-powered alter ego that he can transform into at will.<br /> <br /> Heck, Billy and Shazam are even metaphysically distinct from each other like a Princess's normal and Transformed selves. Remember when the universe got split into adults and children, and Shazam/Billy was used as an intermediary since he could switch freely between them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T05:41:25-07:00","id":1140135,"title":"","content":"Swamp Thing could be a woodblood Ogre Or A Nemesis Beast, with the &quot;Green&quot; being the Lair. I prefer the changeling route, would make him more similar to Beastman (Dual Kith Hunter Heart/Runnerswift Beast), which would make the Red and the Green their respective keepers.<br /> Lobo Looks Like A powerful Anakim Collector to me, or Perhaps a ravager.<br /> Killercroc is another Changeling, Coldscale Ogre. <br /> Scarecrow is a Namtaru Ravager, with a heavy Focus on Nightmares and Lots of Science and occult. Maybe throw in Nightmare Fist. <br /> Aquaman could be a Makara Tyrant, or a mage with life and mind.<br /> Arrow is simply a Hunter. Batman is more likely to be a Beast (Eshmaki Nemsis) or some sort of Darkling, though i prefer the former. Mimir's wisdom would definitly help explaining his (undeniably) Superhuman amount of degrees and detective skills. From the Shadows is obvious, and Epic potential (Strength) is a thing here. Relentless Hunter for the amount of punishment he takes and still goes on.<br /> Bizarro is an abyssal reflection of Superman the obrimos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Written on my phone so random capitalization ftw 09-14-2017, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T06:34:05-07:00","id":1140146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1140135#post1140135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bizarro is an abyssal reflection of Superman the obrimos?</div> </div> </div> </div>But if Superman's a Beast, are abyssal reflections of non-mages a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T07:50:55-07:00","id":1140164,"title":"","content":"Reflection probably isn't the best way to word it but yeah, the Abyss really only tends to target mages because they're its primary method of entry into the world while also attempting to kick it out. Just like spirits, though, they aren't limited to interacting with their main gameline.<br /> <br /> Scarecrow would be a Fear-urged scientist. What he does is entirely mundane, but his psychosis is driven by something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:06:03-07:00","id":1140193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1140164#post1140164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scarecrow would be a Fear-urged scientist. What he does is entirely mundane, but his psychosis is driven by something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon-blooded with Sum of All Fears and a mental Stigmata/Glitch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T10:01:11-07:00","id":1140217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1140193#post1140193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon-blooded with Sum of All Fears and a mental Stigmata/Glitch?</div> </div> </div> </div>An urged is someone with a spirit Fettered to them, using its Influence on them to create an urge in the person, which in this case is to spread fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T10:16:55-07:00","id":1140223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1138733-elseworlds-dc-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1140217#post1140217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An urged is someone with a spirit Fettered to them, using its Influence on them to create an urge in the person, which in this case is to spread fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I'm suggesting a possible alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T10:29:45-07:00","id":1140228,"title":"","content":"He could be an urged Demon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:38:39-07:00","id":1140648,"title":"","content":"Scarecrow fits quite nicely as our local King of Autumn. He adores his autumnal imagery, and uses his onieromancy to wander the minds of the inmates of Arkham for glamour. As a twist, his durance was a mixture of the Scarecrow of Oz and the legend of Ichabod Crane. His keeper was originally the wicked witch of the west, but after the Dorothy incident, ''Elfie'' has lost her Titles, and Crane holds her amnesiac charlatan butt hostage as his glamour-junkie ''sister wife''. The image the player was using was the bad guy in the Crow.<br /> <br /> He works closely with pre-madness Harleen Quinzel, a mage and fellow onieromancer based vaguely on the Cell and Paprika. We have yet to RP the Joker's capture, her attempt to dreamdive, and her subsequent fractured Wisdom, but the idea I will be going for is that her tulpa manifests as the Joker, and various ''pranks'', to contrast the heath ledger style seriousness of the Joker himself. Indeed, one of the big spoiler secret reveals will be that Harley and Joker aren't actually a couple--its all in Harley's head, made real by her tulpa.<br /> <br /> The Penguin is the King of the Winter Court, and so far Gotham's freehold is very mafia esque, even sometimes referring to monarchs as faerie godfathers and godmothers. They're currently trying to fix the Bulwark, by recruiting a Summer Monarch and trying to figure out how to make Poison Ivy crown as Spring Queen.<br /> <br /> I triiiiiiiied to make Swamp Thing a Beast, but the storyline and mechanics simply didn't fit in the slightest. I couldn't give him a spread of powers that fit right, and unlike many other characters, I really wanted Swamp Thing to be visibly disfigured, like Grundy (a promethean). So for Swampy, I'm likely to go with Claimed, by a powerful elemental spirit. The Green and the Red have only been briefly touched on by mages, and as such, the pcs are assuming the Green and Red are ''divisions'' within the Primal Wilds. This may not be far from the truth, who knows yet.<br /> <br /> And btw, my players straight up threatened to QUIT if Batman didn't secretly turn out to be human. I seriously would not recommend trying to do any shenanigans with that idea. I tried doing Beast with him, and it simply ruined the whole feeling and, indeed, the whole POINT of Batman. Even still, most of Gotham assumes him to be a vampire (thanks to Owlman and Manbat, the former being his Strix-possessed ''brother'' Thomas, the latter being a.. well, a vampire with Protean and a bad habit of frenzy). It did result in the almost unheard of situation of a ''mundane human'' being the Apex of Gotham City's Hive. He is well aware of this fact, and plays up on it the best he can.<br /> <br /> As for Superman (technically, Superboy), he ended up....a Solar Exalted XD. Specifically, an Athletics supernal Zenith caste. Powers wise, it fits perfectly, and it makes him the most ''alien'' being I've introduced to the game so far. None of the CofD races really fit his theme well, and him being a remnant of a time and world ''before the Darkness'' gave him a mythic resonance. The Beasts can get Kinship with him, Mages believe him to be the last living Atlanta, Demons think he is the ultimate weapon against the God Machine (well, he DOES punch reality in the face..)..<br /> <br /> <br /> My only sadness is the distinct lack of ''uratha'' type characters in DC. When I started, Bane was going to be a Blood Talon... and then Deviant was revealed as the next gameline. Beast Boy and Vixen were close, but the latter fit better as a Thyrsus. So far our only major werewolf npcs are Universal Movie Monster based, as descendants of the Talbot family. I tacked on Mammoth and Shimmer, but in Shimmer's case it was a stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T11:56:57-07:00","id":1143289,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a nonChroD Superman, somehow. Huh.<br /> <br /> The humanity of Batman is often a point of discussion, about how it defines him and makes his actions more meaningful (btw, I am one of the people that say he absolutely is not a normal human, not even a perfected human. to me he is definitly metahuman. He repeatedly does things far outside the realm of human ability, but that is a topic for another matter) and I see why that is intriguing. So yeah. Keep us updated =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T10:03:44-07:00","id":1203881,"title":"","content":"I just watched this video about how the DC Universe is really a science fiction reality based on divergent geography, and now I want to start working on this again... Damn it DC, release an Unlimited App like Marvel!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"video